# A guide line for the soil showcase, at v = 0.7 metres.
#
# One `u v` pair per line, in metres. See `main_path.spline.ron` for why this is
# a line-based format rather than RON.
#
# Deliberately straight, which is the opposite of what a path wants. A track laid
# on a ruled line reads as ruled; a **comparison chart** has to be ruled, or the
# eye spends its effort on the shape of the boundary instead of on the difference
# between the two soils either side of it.
#
# The spacing is one tile of `soil_showcase`, which is rendered at 70 cm — close
# enough that a two-centimetre clod is a feature rather than a speckle.
-10.00   0.70
 10.00   0.70
